{"created": "2026-10-25T17:49:27.303922+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-31T18:12:12.832376+00:00", "id": 23647165, "conceptrecid": "23647164", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647165", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647164", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23647165", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"A parity frontier between fully renewable electrified and hydrocarbon energy systems: the required EROI under changing final energy demand\"\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23647165", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>Python code that reproduces every number, table and figure of the manuscript &ldquo;A parity frontier between fully renewable electrified and hydrocarbon energy systems: the required EROI under changing final energy demand&rdquo; (Benyahia and Ait Hsain, submitted to Energy), together with the numerical verification of its propositions. The code takes as input the dataset of Aramendia et al. (2024), available at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.25311358. The paper derives, in closed form, the life-cycle EROI that an all-electric supply system, storage and networks included, requires to match hydrocarbons as a function of the growth rate of final energy demand. With 2020 global data, the baseline requirement at 2% annual growth is 5.5.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Benyahia, Georges Ali", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 Mohammed VI Polytechnique"}, {"name": "Ait Hsain, Tareq", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 Mohammed VI Polytechnique"}], "keywords": ["EROI", "Net energy analysis", "Energy transition", "Final energy demand", "Growth", "Useful energy", "Renewable electricity"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.6084/m9.figshare.25311358", "relation": "requires", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1038/s41560-024-01518-6", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "typ